1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,950
Take a photo on your phone, and it lands on your Mac.

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,510
I made a small tool.

3
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:06,170
No more sending it through WeChat,

4
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,570
then downloading it again on the computer.

5
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,170
Open the camera on your phone,

6
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,050
and a preview pops up on your Mac.

7
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:12,380
Paste it straight in.

8
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:14,250
Use it in notes or documents,

9
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,560
or drop it into a chat.

10
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,950
Take several photos without switching back and forth.

11
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,790
They stay together in one group.

12
00:00:19,890 --> 00:00:21,390
Copy the whole group at once.

13
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:23,490
Take a problem you want to understand,

14
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,450
and put it into your study notes.

15
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,440
For experiments or wiring checks,

16
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:30,080
bring the on-site photos into your report.

17
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,730
Portrait or landscape,

18
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:32,840
the original photo is sent.

19
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,470
Pair once, then it reconnects automatically.

20
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:37,590
The Mac keeps the newest twenty images.

21
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:39,180
Older app-managed images are deleted.

22
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,600
Free and open source.

23
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:42,330
The source and install guide

24
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:43,840
are on GitHub.
